ralph/codex-output/iteration-000048-20260519-010141.log:1036:- Verification-suite single-file multi-surface static-test, load-smoke instance (BE-0392 pattern, internal/release/verification_suite_load_smoke_static_test.go + internal/controlplane/httpapi/load_smoke_test.go's new canonical pair TestLoadSmokeContractCoversCoreEndpoints + TestLoadSmokeContractRunsBurstWithStableEnvelopes + SECURITY.md "## Load Smoke Tests" section AND a new row in the Required Verification Gates table + internal/release/AGENTS.md "## Verification suite: load smoke tests (BE-0392)" subsection; FOURTEENTH worked instance of the BE-0379..BE-0391 verification-suite mega-pattern, canonical command `go test -run TestLoadSmoke ./...`, CI step name `Load smoke tests`, verify.sh prefix #17 inserted between BE-0390's #16 and the optionals — optionals renumbered #17→#18 govulncheck, #18→#19 staticcheck, #19→#20 golangci-lint, #20→#21 goreleaser in the SAME edit; TENTH consecutive required-step insertion with optional renumbering since BE-0380's #6). Two BE-0392-specific extensions to the template, all forward-applicable to ANY future verification story whose load-bearing subject is an HTTP handler under burst load: (1) `CANONICAL PAIR ENCODES DETERMINISTIC × DETERMINISTIC DUAL — NO POSTGRES MEMBER` — unlike BE-0389/BE-0390 whose canonical pair splits across deterministic-fixture-only + Postgres-required substrates, BE-0392's BOTH pair members are deterministic. The bootstrap surface (`/healthz`, `/readyz`, `/version`) is the one part of the public HTTP API that needs no backing infrastructure — no Postgres, no fake Dokploy fixtures, no quota counters mutated, no scope-resolution chain. The closed-set member walks an in-memory endpoint table; the burst member spins the test handler in-process via httptest.NewServer and fires 16 workers × 32 iterations = 512 concurrent requests per endpoint. Neither member calls t.Skip on missing env vars — the gate trips on every developer machine and every CI runne