ralph/codex-output/iteration-000093-20260519-061630.log:46467:- HTTP endpoints are data-driven entries in internal/controlplane/httpapi/routes.go newRouteTable: apiRoute{endpoint, handler, resolver}. Authorization is declarative — set openapi.Endpoint.RequiresAuth=true + RequiredAction=string(policy.ActionX), and NewHandler auto-wraps the handler in RequireAuth(authenticator, engine, action, resolver) before registering it, so a served authenticated route is structurally impossible without authorization. TestEveryAuthenticatedRouteHasMappedAction enforces the RequiresAuth<->RequiredAction invariant in CI. The optional apiRoute.resolver derives the policy.Resource from path/query params; leave it nil for self/org-root actions (RequireAuth then authorizes against the principal's own org scope). NewHandler signature is (build, readiness, meta, authenticator, engine, logger); httpapi tests build it through the newTestHandler helper (canned fakeAuthenticator + policy.NewEngine()). Handlers stay thin: read policy.PrincipalFromContext, render via apienvelope.WriteData/WriteError. cmd/yalla-api wires the real stack at startup (pgxpool -> store.New -> store.NewCredentialReader -> auth.NewAuthenticator + policy.NewEngine) and requires YALLA_DATABASE_URL in every profile.
